Here's a comparison of the three major cloud providers:

:::intelligent-ui{v="1"}
root = Comparison("Major cloud providers", [
  {name:"AWS", attributes:["Largest market share (~32%)","Broadest service catalog (200+ services)","Best third-party ecosystem","Often steepest learning curve"]},
  {name:"Microsoft Azure", attributes:["Strong hybrid-cloud (Arc, Stack)","Tight M365 / Enterprise integration","Best for .NET & Windows workloads","Large European presence"]},
  {name:"Google Cloud", attributes:["Leader in data & analytics (BigQuery)","Strongest Kubernetes heritage (GKE)","Competitive pricing (sustained-use discounts)","Smallest of the three but fastest growing"]}
])
:::

**Quick take:** Pick AWS when you want maximum breadth and ecosystem support, Azure when you're already in the Microsoft stack or need hybrid setups, and GCP when data/analytics or Kubernetes are central. Multi-cloud is common, and most teams use a primary provider plus selective services from others.

